specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:12:- `sendStreamEnd` has one call site in `messageHandler.ts`, reached from the `finally` of each turn the handler runs, so a throw anywhere in the run still reaches it unless the turn's socket closed first ([abandon-on-close](../hal-engine-abandon-on-close/spec.md)); `handleUserMessage` sends none ([validated by: ends a provider failure mid-stream with error then stream_end, stream_end last](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L330)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:13:- A provider failing mid-stream produces `error` (`SERVER_ERROR`) then `stream_end`, with `stream_end` the last frame ([validated by: ends a provider failure mid-stream with error then stream_end, stream_end last](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L330)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:14:- A provider rate limit produces `error` (`RATE_LIMITED`) then `stream_end` ([validated by: tells the client to retry when the provider is rate limited](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L311)).
